# Ship after every change

When a code change is finished and ready to test, do not wait to be asked:

1. **Commit** the change (unless the user said not to).
2. **Push** to `origin` (`git push -u origin HEAD` if upstream is missing).
3. **Deploy** with `npm run deploy` so https://blood-analyzer.alexxvives.workers.dev matches local.

GitHub has no deploy workflow — `git push` alone does not update the live Worker.

Skip push/deploy only if the user said the work is local-only, or the change is not meant to ship (notes, aborted work).
